---
title: 16 - DiCoW Inference Sequence Diagram
---
sequenceDiagram
 autonumber
 participant P as Pipeline
 participant B as DiCoW bridge
 participant R as Author runtime child process
 participant DZ as DiariZenPipeline
 participant DC as DiCoWPipeline
 participant HF as Hugging Face Hub / cache
 P->>B: recognize_author(AudioBundle, config, destination)
 B->>B: Validate pinned code commits and clean inference files
 B->>B: Write temporary prepared.wav and request.json
 B->>R: Spawn author Python with dicow_runner.py --request
 alt Oracle RTTM provided
  R->>R: Build annotation from supplied RTTM
 else Predicted diarization
  R->>HF: Load pinned DiariZen + WeSpeaker checkpoints
  R->>DZ: diarizer(full audio)
  DZ-->>R: Annotation
  R->>R: Delete diarizer / gc / clear unused CUDA cache
 end
 R->>R: Normalize labels to SPEAKER_00, SPEAKER_01, ...
 R-->>B: stdout progress event M3
 B-->>P: Progress callback M3
 R->>HF: Load pinned DiCoW model, tokenizer and features
 R->>DC: Construct pipeline with fixed annotation
 R->>DC: preprocess(audio) once, when speakers exist
 DC-->>R: Input features and per-speaker STNO masks
 loop Each target speaker
  R->>DC: _forward(target slice, timestamps, language, beams)
  DC-->>R: Generated tokens
  R->>DC: postprocess_text(decoded timestamp tokens)
  DC-->>R: Timestamped text
 end
 R->>R: Write author-output.json and provenance
 R-->>B: Exit / bridge reads output file
 B->>B: Parse generated timestamps and overlap signals
 B-->>P: DiarizationResult, utterances, metadata, raw
 P->>P: Build TranscriptDocument / write artifacts and joint cache
 Note over R,DC: STNO / FDDT internals belong to pinned upstream code.<br/>No training step or standalone inference network service.
